PROTOTYPE patch for docs/DESIGN_CALL_PROTOCOL.md (section 8). NOT FOR MERGING: measurement only, some bits UNSOUND.
Base: a536f04. Apply with `git apply docs/proto-call-protocol.patch` (git skips this header), build `cargo build --release -p rn-cli`.
Every change is gated by the environment variable RN_PROTO=<bits> (read once, cache::proto_bits()); unset = the base's instructions.
  1   E2 ceiling: self-referencing upvalue folded to the running closure (UNSOUND: no checked entries; fails tests/vm/k6_02_path_switch.lua)
  2   no POLL in lazy-aware traces (UNSOUND)
  4   no BUDGET in lazy-aware traces (UNSOUND: count budgets, instruction-count identity)
  8   E3 conservative direct native return (flush-unsafe: continuation cell / caller base kept in CallInfo.ck / .ctx)
  16  E7 poll placement (no poll in push-through-cell / native-return fragments; the null-cell path gets no poll here)
  64  E1 up-recursion unrolling, k = 2;   128  k = 3 (no adaptive fallback: regresses permute / towers / list)

Workload files used besides bench/ (not committed elsewhere):
--- sumrec.lua ---
    local function sum(n) if n == 0 then return 0 end return n + sum(n - 1) end
    local N = tonumber(arg and arg[1]) or 100000
    local s = 0
    for i = 1, N do s = s + sum(100) end
    print(s)
--- fibu2.lua (one recursion level written inline; same result as bench/programs/fib.lua) ---
    local function fib(n)
      if n < 2 then return n end
      local a, b
      local m = n - 1
      if m < 2 then a = m else a = fib(m - 1) + fib(m - 2) end
      local k = n - 2
      if k < 2 then b = k else b = fib(k - 1) + fib(k - 2) end
      return a + b
    end
    local n = tonumber(arg and arg[1]) or 37
    print(fib(n))

